# A Killer Among Us: "target attacking creature token" (CR 115.1, 601.2c): a token that is not attacking (Human) and an attacking
# creature that is not a token (Llanowar Elves) are not legal targets, so the activation is refused and the enchantment is not
# sacrificed; the attacking Goblin token is legal. Bot2's attacking token would be legal too (any controller): see the Old Hob scenario.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
A Killer Among Us
Llanowar Elves
Forest x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.A Killer Among Us.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Goblin)
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Goblin Token > Bot2; Llanowar Elves > Bot2)
! Bot1.Battlefield.A Killer Among Us.Activate(Target: Bot1.Battlefield.Human Token)
! Bot1.Battlefield.A Killer Among Us.Activate(Target: Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
? Bot1.Battlefield.A Killer Among Us.SecretSubtype = Goblin
Bot1.Battlefield.A Killer Among Us.Activate(Target: Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.A Killer Among Us = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token.Power = 4
Bot1.Battlefield.Human Token.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Power = 1
